Hello, Minions!

Just two days ago, we shared our latest video devlog with you, and we already have a ton of new updates to reveal! And when we say “a lot,” we mean it. As we’re sitting down to write this announcement, we’re not even sure where to begin. So, apologies in advance if this gets a bit chaotic. Without further ado, let’s dive in!

A POLISH(ED) UPDATE

We promised to bring new languages to Be My Horde, and we’re keeping that promise! The first language is now available—our very own Polish! The update is live, and this rollout served as a test run for adding new languages. It helped us refine the process, so you can expect more languages to be implemented more smoothly and quickly in the future. Stay tuned! But for now… zachęcamy naszych rodaków do zagrania w Be My Horde w języku polskim!

But that’s not all. Along with the Polish language, we’re delivering some graphic improvements, fixes, and two things a lot of you were asking for - an optional health bar and keybindings!

Check out the full patch notes below:

💀 New language: Polish;
💀 Added Keybindings;
💀 Added the optional Health Bar;
💀 Accessibility option "Hold to Necromance" changed to "Toggle Instant Cast." When this is available, you need to click a button only once during your run, and Moriana will resurrect minions automatically. Clicking a button a second time turns off automatic resurrection.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44366003/48c08b82b4f0a5f46bafe9e559422fcdad1daa44.gif

ART
💀 Improved the look of the starting location - blood animation added;
💀 Fixed the Vampiric Strike VFX bug;
💀 Fixed the visibility of the experience bar;
💀 Fixed some issues with the crater created by the Sheep explosion;
💀 Fixed the flickering and chromatic aberration in the building animation;
💀 Fixed the bug with Moriana's speed boost VFX.

FIXES:
💀 Fixed the Warriors' animation glitch;
💀 Fixed the range scale with a size that could sometimes cause some units, like Paladins, not to deal damage even when the hammers come in contact with enemies;
💀 Fixed the bug, allowing to resurrect during the Revival animation;
💀 Changes in the pop-up informing about the recommendation of starting a new adventure after the latest update.

UI FIXES:
💀 Improved the perks focus navigation on the second upgrade;
💀 Save slot focus fixed;
💀 Necromancy selection icons repositioned.

BALANCE CHANGES:
💀 Perks descriptions updated;
💀 Updated the chances for certain perks to appear.

OTHER
💀 Changes in the chase and sudden death events movements;
💀 We added the function to record the number of souls in the game, which will help us greatly with potential future crashes. This data will be sent to us with the Unreal Engine Crash Report you send.

MORIANA HAS SOMETHING TO SAY

Recently, we had the incredible opportunity to sit down with none other than Amber Lee Connors! The super-talented voice actress who brings Moriana to (un)life gave us a behind-the-scenes look at her process. We’re excited to share this with you as it offers a closer connection to the world of Be My Horde. Expect more content like this in the future… because bosses need voices, too, right?

[previewyoutube=o81pRnA0QOw;full][/previewyoutube]

MORIANA IN REAL LIFE

We’re beyond excited to announce that from October 25-27, we’ll be attending PGA in Poland, one of the biggest gaming events around! We’ll have our very own booth, complete with playable stations, giveaways, and plenty of time to hang out with visitors. But wait—there’s more… MORIANA HERSELF WILL BE THERE!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44366003/5cda8e63b544bf42ebb7c0bd148442688eb9ee87.png
We’ve teamed up with the incredible cosplayer KAIRI, who will portray Moriana at the event. That’s right, probably the first-ever Moriana cosplay is happening, and we can’t wait to show it off! Be sure to follow Kairi for sneak peeks at her amazing work.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44366003/0c8986dd0c6624387e044bd651f9c7a430753adf.png
If you’re in Poznań, Poland, during the last weekend of October, be sure to visit our booth, meet the team, and grab a photo with the Lady of the Undead herself!

So, to recap: We’ve got the Polish language update along with fixes, an interview with Amber Lee Connors, the PGA announcement, and Moriana cosplay news! We think that’s all for today. Over the next week and a half, we’ll be focused on the event, but shortly after PGA, we hope to have even bigger updates for Be My Horde to share with you.

Stay tuned, and as always, thank you for supporting this little project! Your messages and reviews keep us motivated and moving forward.

Praise be to Moriana!
